> I could believe they both sat before the same fire. You might like to swap some stories with that ol' rabblerouser&#151;
³1revision³122³1tscreate³11074769666³1text_default³1version³21³2ts³21100692276³2ip³2217.247.143.218³2name³2text_default³2data³2summary³3*³3text³3<b>Low Priority Stuff</b> &#150; items that do *not* need an answer or decision this year.

&nbsp;

<b>041117, JunkerIn:</b> Attitude check. As I go along with certain subjects, I think back to certain causes-- now CFR, Bilderberg, etc. Avoid that or put it in as I see it?

<b>040913, Junker:</b> Thank you for the zip & your commendation. I wish too-- perhaps as it grows, it will attract some participants. eBay is handy and has its uses. I would like to see an ancap commerce effort become effective, but I don't yet see how to do that. I'll think on it. Ending, as you know, I appreciate your blog-- well done.

<b>040913, BillStClair:</b> Actually, I <i>haven't</i> been keeping an archive up to now, but I had to copy the whole database in order to move it from netherweb to <nowiki>NearlyFreeSpeech</nowiki>, so I've got it as of 9/11/2004. I put it in billstclair.com/wikidb.zip (about 500K). The pages themselves are in the sub-directories of the "page" directory.

I commend you, Junker, for your work on this Wiki. I wish we could get some other people to participate. My idea of a marketplace never went anywhere, for instance. eBay appears to have the corner on that.

<b>040913, Junker:</b> I am assuming you keep a back-up copy of all this. I don't. Could you provide a zipped, gz'ed, or etc. version of all these pages or is it too much hassle?

<b>040911, Junker:</b> Time flies. Still nobody else here. Shame. This could develop.

<b>040211, Junker:</b> Long story. Internet computer died. Am now finally up on a Linux system. Still no email access. I'm working on that. This one is tons faster & I haven't started channel bundling yet.

Claire Files > Gulching > Gulch Communications. Looking for a place to upload 'alot' of info on uncentralized commo. One suggested here. I think it would fit nicely where I extended computers to packet switching, etc., but it also dovetails into ancap community. I'll add my recommendation to come here & to my site. I have 1000MG of space that needs filling, but no wiki (yet). Regards, J.

<b>040203, Junker:</b> I have become busy at my new site and further so as the new business site comes on-line. I will continue here as and when. I am not abandoning. I still think there is good potential here for items that are needful and helpful. Regards, -J.

<b>040125, Junker:</b> "Junker continues to post large amounts of new content at AnCap Wiki. Thanks, man." And as well, thank *you*.

<b>040124, Junker: Odd artifacts.</b> At <nowiki>TutorGig</nowiki> Encyclopedia on anarcho-capitalism
(http://www.tutorgig.com/encyclopedia/getdefn.jsp?keywords=Anarcho-Capitalism) is

::::"Anarcho-capitalism
:::The neutrality of this article is ." 

Donated from <nowiki>WikipediA</nowiki>?

<b>040123, Junker:</b> I was just, you know, surfin' around&#151;found some words that hark back to the ol' Pat boy himself:

::I have a brain that is trained to think and a heart that loves liberty.
::Those, sir, are the most dangerous weapons on the planet.

I could believe they both sat before the same fire. You might like to swap some stories with that ol' rabblerouser&#151;

::http://www.lewrockwell.com/mcmaken/mcmaken93.html87

